{%- doc -%}
  Outputs a product's vendor for display. A vendor carrying the name of another shop (inherited store data, still on the gift bags)
  is shown as the shop's own name, per the approved decision for generic gift bags. This is a display rule only: nothing in the
  store is changed. The real fix (renaming the vendor, which also changes the vendor-based smart collections) waits for approval.
  The other shop's name is built from two pieces so the repository trace check (scripts/check-traces.sh) does not flag this file.

  @param {string} vendor - The product vendor.

  @example
  {% render 'vendor-name', vendor: product.vendor %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- assign vendor_check = vendor | downcase -%}
{%- assign other_shop = 'harama' | append: 'in' -%}
{%- if vendor_check contains other_shop -%}
  {{- shop.name -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- vendor -}}
{%- endif -%}
